A valid display name can be any string of characters, including control characters.

If the display name contains a control character, then the X server will crash when trying to open the connection.

To fix this issue, we need to make sure that the display name only contains printable ASCII characters.

We can use `isprint()` to check if the character is printable or not.

```c
